his is the same query, but it counts every Claims host instead of filtering down to the silent ones:

fetch dt.entity.host, from:-7d
| fields dt.entity.host = id, hostName = entity.name, tags, lifetime
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| lookup [
    timeseries cpu = avg(dt.host.cpu.usage, scalar: true), by:{dt.entity.host}, from:-24h
    | fields dt.entity.host, cpu
  ], sourceField: dt.entity.host, lookupField: dt.entity.host, prefix: "m."
| summarize totalHosts = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.host),
            reporting  = countDistinctExact(if(isNotNull(m.cpu), dt.entity.host)),
            silent     = countDistinctExact(if(isNull(m.cpu), dt.entity.host))
